    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Unwinding the definitions, we must show that for every compact $U \subset V$ and every map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[ \zeta : ( \bd \Delta ^ m \times \Delta ^ n ) \coprod _{ \bd \Delta ^ m \times \bd \Delta ^ n } ( \Delta ^ m \times \bd \Delta ^ n ) \rightarrow \calF (U) \]
</div>
    <p>
       whose restriction $\zeta | \bd \Delta ^ m \times \Delta ^ n$ is given by $\eta $, there exists a cocompact closed subset $K \subseteq U$ such that $\overline{K} \subseteq X$ has Heyting dimension $< n+m -k$, an open covering $\{  U_{\alpha } \} $ of $U - K$, and a collection of maps 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \zeta _{\alpha }: \Delta ^ m \times \Delta ^ n \rightarrow \calF ( U_{\alpha }) \]
</div>
    <p>
       which extend $\zeta $. This follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/93DA28" data-tag="93DA28">7.2.4.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
